(1. What is a Deadlock?) Tj
0 -18 Td
(A deadlock is a situation where processes are blocked waiting for each others resources.) Tj
0 -25 Td
(2. Necessary Conditions for Deadlock - Coffman Conditions:) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Mutual Exclusion: At least one resource must be non-shareable.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Hold and Wait: A process holds resources while waiting for additional ones.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- No Preemption: Resources cannot be preempted forcibly.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Circular Wait: A closed loop of processes waiting for each other.) Tj
0 -25 Td
(3. Deadlock Handling Strategies:) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Prevention: Invalidate one of Coffman conditions.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Avoidance: Use Bankers Algorithm to ensure safe state.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Detection and Recovery: Resource Allocation Graph and termination.) Tj
0 -25 Td
(4. Critical Section and Mutex:) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Critical section is shared memory access. Mutex ensures mutual exclusion.) Tj
